    "update_time": 1788237927.9003398,
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "**Version A (research-forward)**\n\n> Subject: 30-min chat about how you keep track of research ideas?\n>\n> Hi [Name],\n>\n> I'm David, an HCI PhD student at Virginia Tech (currently on leave and based in SF). I'm studying how researchers keep track of their thinking across notes, papers and AI chats, and where ideas get lost.\n>\n> Would you be open to a 30-minute conversation in the next two weeks? It's not a sales pitch. I'm trying to understand real workflows, and I'm happy to share what I learn from other researchers.\n>\n> I came across your work on [specific paper/topic], which is why I thought of you.\n>\n> Thanks,\n> David Barron\n\n**Version B (shorter, more casual)**\n\n> Subject: quick research chat?\n>\n> Hi [Name], I'm an HCI PhD student (Virginia Tech, on leave in SF) talking to researchers about how they keep track of ideas across notes, papers and AI chats. Would you have 30 minutes sometime in the next two weeks? Happy to work around your schedule, in person in Berkeley or on Zoom.\n>\n> David\n\nVersion A will do better with faculty-adjacent folks; B with PhD students. Personalize the one specific line, since that's what gets replies."
     ]
    },
